"confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 424507, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BQ3WZvVyHM1r9Y1qY4vwJS", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_timeout"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 424507, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BQ3WZvVyHM1r9Y1qY4vwJS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 430428, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I've opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own comment says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed that one setting to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe PR description has a mistake I couldn't fix, because I don't have a way to edit PRs. It says 2.665 \"now round[s] to 2.66 instead of 2.68,\" but the old code gave 2.67. Please correct that line on the PR.\n\nI also couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system didn't recognise that ID. So the fix is based on what the test expects and the code comment, not the advisory itself.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01K1eAv8MiHBZLcH1Y6tYpZE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016j5QLA8RMghMDrGxe3fUg3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LF7aibRbGRcNG42LsMUE3S", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017JtS4QKH1xYm5vhvRCRidv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018DfomBtGyPjSNTLUqNW1sd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MNbL6vmNhqMY9YZfhZ5hdM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-round-half-even", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-round-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011jghhzzHEG4rF6oD84PAkD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BQ3WZvVyHM1r9Y1qY4vwJS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-round-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (despite its docstring saying ROUND_HALF_EVEN).\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Values like 2.665 now round to 2.66 instead of 2.68.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I've opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own comment says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`).\n- **The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed that one setting to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe PR description has a mistake I couldn't fix, because I don't have a way to edit PRs. It says 2.665 \"now round[s] to 2.66 instead of 2.68,\" but the old code gave 2.67. Please correct that line on the PR.\n\nI also couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system didn't recognise that ID. So the fix is based on what the test expects and the code comment, not the advisory itself.\n\nThe PR hasn't been merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}